<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crevillent</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crevillent is a town at the foot of the Sierra de Crevillent in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alicante">Alicante</a>, Valencian Community, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> came under Castilian overlordship in the 1240s, it remained an autonomous Muslim lordship under the Banu Hudayr family until about 1318, when it was absorbed into the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>. Its Muslim population survived as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudejar">Mudéjars</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Moriscos</a> until the expulsion of 1609.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crevillent.jpg" alt="Crevillent" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Quesada at Spanish Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CrevillentIglesia.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
